{
  "claims": [
    {
      "text": "The four-limb test in POL-NS-01 fails on the platform's own telemetry, so no no-show fee is chargeable against this rider. Limb (a) is met only in form - an 'arrived' event is stamped at 11:12:40. Limb (b) then fails: across 84 driver fixes the closest approach to the pickup pin is 298.04 m (derived.driver_track.min_distance_m), so the trace never places the driver inside the 50 m STANDARD arrival radius at or before that event. Limb (c) fails: the longest qualifying in-geofence run is 0.0 s against the 300 s STANDARD minimum, a 300 s shortfall (derived.arrival.longest_qualifying_run.duration_sec; derived.arrival.shortfall_sec), and the trip record's own wait_time_min is 1.0 minute - itself well under the 300 s the clause requires. Limb (d) fails: the trip is closed as COMPLETED with cancelled_at, cancelled_by and cancellation_reason_code all null, so there is no driver termination on RIDER_NO_SHOW, RIDER_UNREACHABLE or EXCESSIVE_WAIT. The ledger is consistent with that - the cancellation_fee line is 0.00.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-GPS-00704", "EV-TRIP-00704", "EV-FARE-00704"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-NS-01"],
      "relies_on": "derived.arrival.qualifying_fix_count",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "POL-NS-02 allows an arrival finding only where the trace carries at least three consecutive fixes inside the 50 m STANDARD radius at 25 m accuracy or better. The derived arrival block reports qualifying_fix_count 0 and longest_qualifying_run.fix_count 0 across 84 fixes, so there is no qualifying in-radius fix anywhere in the 15 minutes preceding the end of the trip, POL-NS-01 limb (b) fails outright, and the full refund of the cancellation fee that the clause directs is triggered. The closest the driver ever came, 298.04 m, is also inside POL-NS-03's 400 m wrong-entrance ceiling, so this cannot be dressed as a POL-NS-01 arrival at the pin on either route.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-GPS-00704", "EV-TRIP-00704"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-NS-02", "POL-NS-03", "POL-NS-01"],
      "relies_on": "derived.arrival.qualifying_fix_count",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "Even if the 11:12:40 marker were taken at face value, the effective in-geofence dwell is 0 s against the 300 s STANDARD minimum - a 300 s shortfall - so under POL-NS-06 the fee is not chargeable and is refunded in full, whether or not the rider was present. The LTA CLOSURE advisory on the Canal-side access road does not rescue the charge: POL-NS-06(i) permits separate in-geofence intervals to be summed only where an admissible advisory covers the pickup road and the waiting window, but this trace has no in-geofence intervals to sum at all (derived.arrival.accumulated_dwell.run_count 0; longest_run_sec 0.0), and limb (ii) is express that an advisory never reduces the required minimum and never excuses a shortfall on its own.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-GPS-00704", "EV-ADVIS-00704-01", "EV-FARE-00704"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-NS-06", "POL-NS-01"],
      "relies_on": "derived.arrival.accumulated_dwell.shortfall_sec",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The chat log shows the trip ended with the rider still in the vehicle and still asking to be carried on: at 11:24:20 the rider wrote 'Why are you making me get out before the destination?' and at 11:24:50 the driver answered 'Water too deep; I will end here.' On the parties' own statements this is a driver-side termination mid-route. Nothing in the record says the rider failed to board, could not be reached, or caused an excessive wait, so POL-NS-01 limb (d) cannot be made out and the no-show fee machinery has no subject matter on this trip at all.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-CHAT-00704", "EV-TRIP-00704"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-NS-01"],
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The SGD 14.20 the rider contests is the completed-trip platform fare, not a no-show charge: the ledger itemises base 3.80 + distance 6.05 + time 3.55 + platform fee 0.80 = 14.20, with cancellation_fee 0.00 and a trip closed as COMPLETED. Any charge this category could fix is capped by fee_schedule.resolution_rule at the greater of the STANDARD zone fee (4.00) and the RYDE_X vehicle-tier fee (4.00). A no-show figure of 14.20 is not an amount this policy can produce, and the ledger records no no-show line against the rider; the amount actually at issue is the fare, which is why the disposition must be assessed on the real complaint and not on a fee that does not exist.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-FARE-00704", "EV-TRIP-00704"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-NS-01", "POL-GEN-03"],
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "POL-NS-07 compensation presupposes that POL-NS-01 is satisfied in full and that no clause from POL-NS-03 to POL-NS-06 displaces it. Neither holds here: limbs (b), (c) and (d) of POL-NS-01 all fail, and POL-NS-06 independently makes the fee refundable, so no driver compensation is payable and the rider cannot be made to fund an 80 per cent payout on a fee that was never chargeable. The rider's exposure on this category is nil, not the SGD 14.20 in dispute.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-GPS-00704", "EV-TRIP-00704", "EV-FARE-00704"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-NS-07", "POL-NS-01", "POL-NS-06"],
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The only artifact that proves what the rider was actually charged is the fare ledger, and it does not reconcile with the schedule for this trip: its cancellation-fee line is 0.00, while the figure produced by fee_schedule.resolution_rule for a STANDARD pickup and a RYDE_X vehicle is the greater of 4.00 and 4.00, and the platform's own derived money block publishes the gap as difference -4.00, with fee_charged 0.00 against schedule_fee 4.00. POL-NS-08(d) makes a fare line that does not equal the resolution-rule amount an impaired fare_breakdown, and POL-NS-08 sets its own policy-level thresholds, so the pre-pass 'COMPLETE' tag at weight 1.0 does not close the question. Where the amount at issue is proved only by that artifact, the ruling may not exceed PARTIAL_REFUND and the case escalates under POL-NS-09; escalation is terminal and the SGD 14.20 is held rather than collected - the only disposition on this record that does not leave the rider carrying a charge this category cannot justify, and the only one that hands the reviewer the early-termination complaint that a NO_ACTION would leave unanswered.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-FARE-00704", "EV-TRIP-00704", "EV-GPS-00704"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-NS-08", "POL-NS-09", "POL-GEN-02"],
      "relies_on": "derived.money.difference"
    },
    {
      "text": "No abuse trigger under POL-NS-09(c) or (d) is present, and none should be imputed from profile history. rider_profile.no_show_disputes_30d is 0, and rider_profile.disputes_with_counterparty_90d and driver_profile.disputes_with_counterparty_90d are 0 and 0, so there are no repeat no-show disputes between these two parties in the trailing 90 days. Those are the only profile fields those limbs read (POL-GEN-01); ratings, account ages, lifetimes and cancellation rates are context only. If this case escalates, it should escalate on the fare-integrity defect, not on anyone's conduct record.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-RPROF-00704", "EV-DPROF-00704"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-NS-09", "POL-GEN-01"],
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    }
  ]
}

{
  "claims": [
    {
      "text": "The SGD 14.20 the rider contests is the fare of a COMPLETED trip, not a no-show or cancellation fee. The payments ledger itemises base fare 3.80 + distance fare 6.05 (5.8 km at 0.75/km) + time fare 3.55 (13.0 min at 0.28/min) + platform fee 0.80, which totals 14.20, and it carries cancellation_fee 0.00, waiting_time_fee 0 and no no-show line at all. The no-show complaint therefore attacks a charge the ledger does not contain: whatever route the rider pleads, there is no cancellation fee on this trip for him to recover.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-FARE-00704", "EV-TRIP-00704"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-NS-01", "POL-GEN-03"],
      "relies_on": "fare_breakdown.cancellation_fee",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "This is a completed journey, not a driver-terminated no-show, so the charge framework of POL-NS-01 was never engaged in the first place: the trip record shows status COMPLETED, cancelled_at null, cancelled_by null and cancellation_reason_code null, with accepted and arrived at 11:12:40, started 11:13:40 and ended 11:26:40. Limb (d) of POL-NS-01 requires the trip to have been terminated by the driver under RIDER_NO_SHOW, RIDER_UNREACHABLE or EXCESSIVE_WAIT, and no such event exists; equally, no clause from POL-NS-02 to POL-NS-06 touches anything but the cancellation-fee line, which is 0.00. Under POL-GEN-03 the present state stands: the trip fare is CHARGED and refund_issued_sgd is 0.00, and the rider's claim is not supported by this record.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-TRIP-00704", "EV-FARE-00704"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-NS-01", "POL-GEN-03"],
      "relies_on": "trip_record.status",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "Both parties' accounts of the termination agree, and the platform's own third-party advisory corroborates them. LTA recorded a HIGH-severity CLOSURE of the Canal-side access road for flash flooding, active from 10:43:40 to 11:56:40 — a window that covers the trip and overlaps it by 13.0 minutes — with intersects_route true. The in-app chat shows the driver giving the reason as it happened: 'Water too deep; I will end here' at 11:24:50, thirty seconds after the rider's question at 11:24:20. POL-NS-06 is the clause under which this category gives a road closure an operative role, and CLOSURE is a recognised admissible advisory type under it; the early end of the journey was an externally imposed flood closure, not a driver default.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-ADVIS-00704-01", "EV-CHAT-00704", "EV-TRIP-00704"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-NS-06"],
      "relies_on": "traffic_advisory.overlap_minutes",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The driver's GPS trace is complete and unimpaired, and it matches the trip record: 84 fixes at a 10-second cadence from 11:12:50 to 11:26:40, coverage 100%, max_gap_sec 0.0, trace_distance_km 5.81 against the record's actual_distance_km 5.8 over 13.0 minutes, and an actual 5.8 km against the routing engine's 6.0 km optimal (-3.3 per cent). The fare charged is therefore supported by distance and time actually driven, and the journey covered essentially the whole of the intended route distance — a profile that leaves no room for the suggestion of an abandoned hire.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-GPS-00704", "EV-TRIP-00704"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-NS-01", "POL-GEN-03"],
      "relies_on": "derived.driver_track.fix_count",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The rider's single chat message does not open the rider-exonerating route in POL-NS-04. Limb (a) requires a message during the waiting window that is locating or coordinating — the rider's own position, an entrance, block, tower or bay, a request for the driver's position, or a statement that the rider cannot see the vehicle; 'Why are you making me get out before the destination?' is none of those. Limb (b) also fails, because the driver did reply, at 11:24:50, thirty seconds after the rider's message and well inside the 120-second window, and his reply states the reason for the termination rather than acknowledging a coordination failure. Limb (c) could not be run in any event, since the trace carries no rider track at all.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-CHAT-00704", "EV-GPS-00704", "EV-TRIP-00704"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-NS-04"],
      "relies_on": "derived.rider_presence.available",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "There is no abuse pattern on this record to escalate. Under POL-NS-07's anti-farming check, driver_profile.no_show_terminations_30d is 1, below the four-termination limb, and 1 divided by driver_profile.completed_trips_30d of 110 is 0.009, far below the 0.08 rate limb, so that check does not trip and POL-NS-09(d) is not engaged; rider_profile.no_show_disputes_30d is 0, and rider and driver each show disputes_with_counterparty_90d of 0, so POL-NS-09(c) is not engaged either. The only reason no driver compensation is claimed under POL-NS-07 is that no cancellation fee was ever itemised on this trip for the 80 per cent rate to be applied to — the SGD 14.20 at issue is trip fare, and its disposition is NO_ACTION.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-DPROF-00704", "EV-RPROF-00704", "EV-FARE-00704"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-NS-07", "POL-NS-09"],
      "relies_on": "driver_profile.no_show_terminations_30d",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    }
  ]
}

