  "ruling": {
    "ruling": "NO_ACTION",
    "amount_sgd": null,
    "driver_compensation_sgd": null,
    "referrals": [],
    "confidence": 0.88,
    "explanation": "Both parties: the SGD 14.20 in dispute is the fare of a completed trip, not a no-show or cancellation fee, so there is nothing in this category to refund. The payments ledger itemises the SGD 14.20 as base fare SGD 3.80 + distance fare SGD 6.05 + time fare SGD 3.55 + platform fee SGD 0.80, and its cancellation-fee line is SGD 0.00. The trip record shows a COMPLETED trip (started 11:13:40, ended 11:26:40, 5.8 km in 13.0 min, against an optimal 6.0 km, a deviation of -3.3%) with cancelled_at, cancelled_by and cancellation_reason_code all null, so POL-NS-01 limb (d) is not met and no no-show fee was ever chargeable. Every refund route in the category — POL-NS-01, POL-NS-02, POL-NS-05 and POL-NS-06 — operates only on the cancellation-fee line, which is SGD 0.00, so none of them moves money, and POL-NS-07 driver compensation is unavailable because it presupposes POL-NS-01 satisfied in full, which this completed trip does not satisfy. The rider's account of the trip is substantially borne out: he walked to the car (the driver's closest approach to the pin was 298.04 m, so he never entered the 50 m STANDARD geofence), the trip ended early under the LTA CLOSURE advisory on the Canal-side access road (active 10:43:40 to 11:56:40, overlapping the trip by 13.0 minutes), and the driver wrote 'Water too deep; I will end here' at 11:24:50. That is a genuine service/route complaint, but it lies outside the NO_SHOW_CHARGE category, and these clauses can refund only a cancellation fee, not a completed-trip fare. To the driver: no fee and no compensation arise, and the fare as charged is supported by the distance and time actually driven.\n\nI reject the rider's fare-integrity argument. The contention that POL-NS-08(d) is engaged because the ledger's cancellation-fee line (SGD 0.00) differs from the SGD 4.00 that fee_schedule.resolution_rule produces for a STANDARD pickup and a RYDE_X vehicle (the ledger's own derived 'difference' of -4.00) does not hold: the resolution-rule figure is the amount of a chargeable cancellation fee, no cancellation fee was chargeable on this completed trip, and the SGD 0.00 line is therefore correct and reconciles. There is no fare defect, no impairment to cap confidence, and no POL-NS-09(e) escalation. No other escalation trigger fires either: the records agree on arrival, dwell and completion, so POL-NS-09(b) is not engaged, and the profile checks show driver no_show_terminations_30d of 1 against completed_trips_30d of 110 (rate 0.009), with no_show_disputes_30d and disputes_with_counterparty_90d of 0 on both sides, so neither POL-NS-09(c) nor POL-NS-09(d) is engaged. Rating, account-age and lifetime fields are context only (POL-GEN-01) and were given no weight. The present state therefore stands and the disputed charge is left as it is; if the rider wishes to pursue the early-termination complaint, that must be raised outside the no-show category."
  },
  "discarded_claims": []
}

{
  "ruling": {
    "ruling": "NO_ACTION",
    "amount_sgd": null,
    "driver_compensation_sgd": null,
    "referrals": [],
    "confidence": 0.8,
    "explanation": "To both parties — the outcome. The SGD 14.20 the rider contests is the platform fare for a completed trip, not a no-show or cancellation fee, and no cancellation fee was charged on this trip. The ledger reads base fare 3.80 + distance fare 6.05 (5.8 km at 0.75/km) + time fare 3.55 (13.0 min at 0.28/min) + platform fee 0.80 = 14.20, and its cancellation-fee line is 0.00; the trip record closes the trip as COMPLETED with cancelled_at, cancelled_by and cancellation_reason_code all null. There is therefore no cancellation fee to refund, and the fare is supported by distance and time actually driven (5.8 km / 13.0 min against a 6.0 km / 14 min optimal). The present state stands.\n\nTo the rider, on the no-show tests you raised: they do fail, but they fail against a fee that was never charged. The GPS trace (84 fixes, 100 percent coverage, no gaps) puts the driver's closest approach to the pickup pin at 298.04 m, with 0 qualifying in-geofence fixes and a longest qualifying run of 0.0 s against the 300 s STANDARD minimum, so POL-NS-01 limbs (b) and (c) are not satisfied and POL-NS-02's full-refund direction and POL-NS-06's 300 s shortfall direction both apply — but each of those clauses refunds the cancellation-fee line only, and that line is 0.00. A full refund of a 0.00 charge returns nothing. The driver's 'arrived' marker is not caught by POL-NS-05 either: the closest approach (298.04 m) is just under the 300 m false-arrival threshold, so no false-arrival referral is produced.\n\nTo the rider, on the fare-integrity point: I do not accept that POL-NS-08(d) is engaged. That limb compares the ledger's cancellation-fee line with the amount produced by fee_schedule.resolution_rule, and the resolution rule fixes the chargeable cancellation fee — the greater of the STANDARD zone-class fee (4.00) and the RYDE_X vehicle-tier fee (4.00) — where a cancellation fee is chargeable. This trip completed, so no cancellation fee was chargeable and 0.00 is the correct line. The derived money block's schedule_fee 4.00, fee_charged 0.00 and difference -4.00 simply record that the no-show schedule would have been 4.00 while nothing was charged; the negative difference shows the rider was not charged a no-show fee at all, not that the ledger is defective. The fare_breakdown is not impaired, no 'sole evidence' question arises, and POL-NS-09(e) is not engaged.\n\nOn driver compensation: POL-NS-07 requires POL-NS-01 to be satisfied in full and no clause from POL-NS-03 to POL-NS-06 to displace it. Neither holds — limbs (b), (c) and (d) of POL-NS-01 fail, and there is no cancellation fee for the 80 percent rate to apply to — so no driver compensation is payable. The anti-farming check does not trip (no_show_terminations_30d 1, below 4; 1/110 = 0.009, below 0.08) and the repeat-dispute test is not met (disputes_with_counterparty_90d 0 and 0), so POL-NS-09(c) and (d) are not engaged. Both parties' accounts of the early end agree and are corroborated by the LTA CLOSURE advisory on the Canal-side access road (active 10:43:40 to 11:56:40, overlapping the trip by 13.0 minutes) and the driver's in-app message 'Water too deep; I will end here'; I have taken that as context, not as a ground for payment.\n\nOne question this category cannot answer, which I leave open for the platform rather than raise as a referral: whether the early end of the journey when the access road flooded gives the rider any remedy for a cut-short trip. No clause in the NO_SHOW_CHARGE category refunds a completed-trip fare, so no clause produces a referral here; POL-NS-05(ii) is not triggered (298.04 m is inside the 300 m threshold) and no other clause adds one."
  },
  "discarded_claims": []
}

{
  "ruling": {
    "ruling": "NO_ACTION",
    "amount_sgd": null,
    "driver_compensation_sgd": null,
    "referrals": [],
    "confidence": 0.9,
    "explanation": "The SGD 14.20 you are contesting is the fare for a trip that was actually run, not a no-show or cancellation fee, so the no-show framework has no fee to refund. The payments ledger builds the 14.20 as base fare 3.80 + distance fare 6.05 (5.8 km at 0.75/km) + time fare 3.55 (13.0 min at 0.28/min) + platform fee 0.80, and its cancellation-fee line is 0.00. The trip record closes the trip as COMPLETED with cancelled_at, cancelled_by and cancellation_reason_code all null. On the no-show question the parties are in substance agreed: the four conditions of POL-NS-01 are not met. The driver's trace (84 fixes, coverage 100%, max gap 0.0 s) never places him inside the 50 m STANDARD pickup radius - his closest approach was 298.04 m - so limbs (b) and (c) fail (in-geofence dwell 0 s against the 300 s minimum, a 300 s shortfall), and limb (d) fails because the trip was not terminated under RIDER_NO_SHOW, RIDER_UNREACHABLE or EXCESSIVE_WAIT. But those failures operate on the cancellation-fee line, and that line is 0.00. The rider's claims that POL-NS-02 and POL-NS-06 direct a 'full refund' are therefore accepted in form but move no money: the refund they direct is a refund of a fee that was never charged. The driver's own account - 'there was no cancellation fee' - matches the ledger, and the LTA CLOSURE advisory on the Canal-side access road (active 10:43:40-11:56:40, overlapping the trip by 13.0 minutes) together with the in-app exchange (rider 11:24:20, driver 11:24:50 'Water too deep; I will end here') explains the early end. The trace shows 5.8 km against the routing engine's 6.0 km optimal route, so the distance actually driven was essentially the whole intended route and the fare reflects service provided. The argument that the fare breakdown is impaired under POL-NS-08(d) - its cancellation-fee line 0.00 against the schedule figure of 4.00 (the greater of the STANDARD zone fee and the RYDE_X vehicle-tier fee) - and that the case must therefore escalate, is rejected: even taking that reconciliation gap at face value, the fare breakdown is not the ONLY evidence for the deciding fact, because the trip record independently establishes a completed trip with no cancellation, so POL-NS-08's escalation sentence does not engage and POL-NS-09(e) does not fire. Nor do POL-NS-09(b) (the arrival-marker question is resolved by POL-NS-02/NS-05, not left contradictory), (c) or (d) (rider and driver each show 0 counterparty disputes in 90 days; the anti-farming test is 1 no-show termination against 110 completed trips, far below the 4-termination / 0.08 rate limbs). POL-NS-04 does not apply - the driver replied 30 seconds after the rider's message, inside the 120-second window - and no driver compensation is payable under POL-NS-07, which requires POL-NS-01 to be satisfied in full and there is no cancellation fee for the 80 percent rate to apply to. Result: the rider's claim is not supported and the present state stands, with the SGD 14.20 completed-trip fare unchanged and no refund or compensation ordered. For the rider's benefit: if the underlying grievance is that the journey was cut short by the flood rather than by any fault of his own, that is a service complaint about a completed trip, which this no-show category cannot price; it should be raised with support under the correct category, as no clause here produces a refund of a completed-trip fare."
  },
  "discarded_claims": []
}
